# A virtual Clock: no `@` lines, a deadline wait returning the prompt at
# once, background lines at `:clock advance`, a redefinition while a Run is
# suspended, and a Clock that never goes backwards.
> :clock virtual 2026-09-30T10:00:00Z
> :clock
virtual 2026-09-30T10:00:00Z
> put 0 into ticks
> on tick
|   wait 5 s
|   add 1 to ticks
|   say "tick " & ticks
| end tick
> tick and wait
> :clock advance 2 s
> :clock advance 3 s
[session/r2] tick 1
> send tick to session
> send tick to session
> :clock advance 5 s
[session/r4] tick 2
[session/r6] tick 3
# Redefining the Handler discards the Run suspended in it, and carries
# `ticks` over.
> send tick to session
> on tick
|   add 10 to ticks
| end tick
! discarded session/r8
> :clock advance 10 s
> tick
> ticks
13
> :clock
virtual 2026-09-30T10:00:20Z
> :clock virtual 2026-09-30T09:00:00Z
! clock backwards
> :clock advance 1 GBP
! bad arguments
> :clock real
> :clock advance 1 s
! clock is real
